    "result_text": "The test passes.\n\nThe change request \u2014 \"the money I am owed should only count invoices I have actually sent; do not count drafts\" \u2014 was a one-line fix in the server-side aggregate. The dashboard's outstanding total was filtering on a stale `status = 'UNPAID'` value, left over from before the invoice lifecycle moved to DRAFT \u2192 SENT \u2192 PAID. I updated `DashboardRepository.summary()` to sum only `status = 'SENT'` invoices, which correctly excludes both DRAFT (not yet sent) and PAID (already settled).\n\nNo schema change or front-end change was needed: the `status` column and the `dashboard-outstanding-total` element already exist, and the seed endpoint already accepts arbitrary statuses. The Playwright spec confirms the total is `$300.00` (the two SENT invoices), excluding the $50 draft and $30 paid.",
